# Writing Docs, Linter Rules & Using `acdd lint`

ACDD treats documentation and architectural boundaries as **machine-checkable contracts**, not passive prose. This guide explains how to structure Markdown documentation, write enforceable linter rules, and run `acdd lint` in daily workflows and CI.

---

## 1. How to write ACDD-indexed documentation

Add every documentation file or directory you want indexed under `docs:` in `acdd.yaml`.

### YAML frontmatter
Start every Markdown file at byte 0 with valid YAML frontmatter:

```yaml
---
title: "Billing Ledger Architecture"
doc_type: architecture
---
```

`doc_type` powers filtered search via `search_docs(doc_type="...")`.

### Heading chunking (BM25 sections)
Use clear `##` and `###` headings. ACDD splits every document at headings into independent `DocSection` units indexed into SQLite FTS5/BM25.

### Verified symbol links (code claims)
When referencing a real code declaration, use its **exact indexed declaration name** and optionally link to its owning source file to disambiguate:

```markdown
Transactions are committed inside [`record_entry`](../src/billing/ledger.rs).
```

- ACDD resolves candidate claims against eligible declarations in `.acdd/code-map.sqlite`.
- Only a **unique** match creates a verified documentation edge (`code_map_inspect` / `code_map_explain` surface verified sections alongside the symbol).
- Never invent qualified paths or approximate names — broken symbol claims are flagged by `acdd lint` (`docs.broken_symbol_claim`).

### Declaring architectural invariants (`INV-*`)
To register an architectural invariant that ACDD prioritizes during `code_map_impact` and injects into `ClaimResp` (`docs.invariants`):

1. Place its `INV-*` ID inside a GitHub alert callout (`[!IMPORTANT]`, `[!WARNING]`, `[!NOTE]`) or invariant list.
2. Include an exact source symbol link (creating a `governs` edge) **or** pair it with an executable `acdd-rule` block (`invariant: INV-...`).
3. Keep each canonical `INV-*` definition in **one** file — duplicate non-contract `INV-*` IDs fail `docs.duplicate_invariant`, and unlinked invariants fail `docs.orphan_invariant`.

```markdown
> [!IMPORTANT]
> - INV-BILLING-TX-SINGLE-OWNER: Only `BillingRepo` may open ledger write transactions. [`BillingRepo`](../src/billing/repo.rs)
```

*(Wrap illustrative `INV-*` examples inside fenced code blocks so the scanner ignores them.)*

### Relative links
Use workspace-relative Markdown links (`../reference/cli.md#section`). Validate all links and heading anchors anytime with:

```sh
acdd docs check
```

---

## 2. How to write linter rules

Architectural rules can be declared in **two places**:
1. Centrally in **`.acdd/lint/*.yaml`** (configured via `lint_dirs:` in `acdd.yaml`) under `zones:` and `rules:`.
2. Inline inside **non-archive Markdown docs** as fenced **` ```acdd-rule `** YAML blocks — keeping the rule right next to the `INV-*` invariant it enforces.

### Defining zones and complexity limits in `.acdd/lint/zones.yaml`

```yaml
complexity:
  severity: warn
  invariant: INV-BOUNDED-STRUCTURAL-COMPLEXITY
  max_file_prod_lines: 800
  max_file_prod_lines_error: 1850
  max_cognitive_complexity: 25

zones:
  domain:
    - "src/domain/**"
  storage:
    - "src/storage/**"
  api:
    - "src/api/**"
```

### The 8 `ArchRuleKind` primitives

#### 1. `allow_only_dependencies`
Restricts outgoing dependencies from `from` strictly to `to`:
```yaml
- id: ARCH-DOMAIN-LEAF
  severity: error
  kind: allow_only_dependencies
  from: { zones: [domain] }
  to: { zones: [] }
  message: "src/domain must remain a pure leaf with zero upward dependencies"
```

#### 2. `forbid_dependency`
Bans specific internal zones or external symbols/crates:
```yaml
- id: ARCH-API-NO-RAW-SQL
  severity: error
  kind: forbid_dependency
  from: { zones: [api] }
  to:
    zones: [storage]
    external_symbols: ["sqlx", "rusqlite"]
  message: "API handlers must call domain services instead of storage or SQL drivers directly"
```

#### 3. `single_owner`
Confines an external dependency or capability to designated `owner_paths`:
```yaml
- id: ARCH-SQLITE-OWNER
  severity: error
  kind: single_owner
  to:
    external_symbols: ["rusqlite"]
  owner_paths: ["src/storage/**"]
  message: "rusqlite usage is confined to src/storage/**"
```

#### 4. `boundary_entry`
Requires external callers targeting `to.paths` to enter only through explicit `entrypoints`:
```yaml
- id: ARCH-PIPELINE-ENTRY
  severity: error
  kind: boundary_entry
  to: { paths: ["src/pipeline/**"] }
  entrypoints: ["src/pipeline/mod.rs", "src/pipeline/runner.rs"]
  message: "Callers must enter src/pipeline through mod.rs or runner.rs"
```

#### 5. `ast_pattern`
Matches Tree-sitter AST patterns (supporting `$VAR` metavariables) in selected paths and languages:
```acdd-rule
id: INV-NO-RAW-GIT
invariant: INV-NO-RAW-GIT
severity: error
kind: ast_pattern
from:
  paths: ["src/**", "crates/**"]
  exclude_paths: ["crates/acdd-core/src/git.rs"]
  languages: ["rust"]
ast_pattern: 'Command::new("git")'
include_tests: false
message: "Spawn git only through acdd_core::git"
```

#### 6. `forbid_cycles`
Rejects dependency cycles across specified zones/depths (`depth >= 1`):
```yaml
- id: ARCH-NO-ZONE-CYCLES
  severity: error
  kind: forbid_cycles
  zones: [domain, storage, api]
  depth: 4
```

#### 7. `must_implement`
Requires matching types/declarations in `from` to implement or inherit `to`:
```yaml
- id: ARCH-PROVIDERS-IMPL-TRAIT
  severity: error
  kind: must_implement
  from: { paths: ["src/providers/**"] }
  to: { symbols: ["DomainProvider"] }
```

#### 8. `doc_integrity`
Enforces strict documentation checks (`broken_doc_link`, `broken_symbol_claim`, `orphan_invariant`, `duplicate_invariant`) on matching doc paths:
```yaml
- id: ARCH-DOCS-STRICT
  severity: error
  kind: doc_integrity
  from: { paths: ["docs/adr/**", "docs/architecture/**"] }
```

---

## 3. How to use `acdd lint` & `code_map_lint`

### CLI usage

```sh
# Default sweep (arch, syntax, docs) across the whole workspace
acdd lint

# Full hygiene sweep including clones, dead tails, and cycles
acdd lint --categories all

# Scope to one directory or file, filter by category/rule/severity
acdd lint src/billing/ --categories arch,duplicates,dead_tails --severity error
acdd lint --rule INV-NO-RAW-GIT
```

### MCP usage (`code_map_lint`)
Agents invoke `code_map_lint` with optional `target`, `categories`, `rules`, `severity`, and pagination (`limit`, `offset`, `generation`).

### Enforcing lint automatically in workflow gates
Attach `code.lint` to any `build` or `verify` gate inside `.acdd/workflows/default.yaml`:

```yaml
gates_patch:
  - id: tasks.build
    checks:
      - code.seam
      - check: code.lint
        with:
          categories: [arch, syntax, docs, duplicates]
```

And pair gate checks with `code_map_query(operation="duplicates")` / `code_map_query(operation="dead_tails")` during review to prevent clones and dead code from entering `main`.
